      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Microorganisms – Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Microorganisms are classified into major groups: Bacteria, Viruses, Fungi, Protozoa, and Algae.",
        "Useful microorganisms play essential roles in fermentation, decomposition, nitrogen fixation, and antibiotic production.",
        "Communicable diseases are caused by infectious pathogens transmitted via air, water, direct contact, or vectors.",
        "Non-communicable diseases stem from lifestyle choices, genetic factors, or nutritional deficiencies.",
        "Vaccines stimulate the immune system to build active immunity, whereas antibiotics specifically target bacterial cell walls or processes."
      ],
      "id": "hh4mkay"
