    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "SSC exams frequently ask to distinguish between bacterial diseases (e.g., Tuberculosis, Cholera) and viral diseases (e.g., Polio, Measles, Dengue).",
        "Antibiotics are effective against bacteria but completely ineffective against viruses.",
        "Remember key commercial/agricultural microbes: Lactobacillus converts milk into curd, while Rhizobium fixes atmospheric nitrogen in leguminous plants."
      ],
